Call dynamically registered callbacks as what they are: WebAssembly checks the type of every call
through a pointer, and C code commonly registers a function of another type than the one called
(a GDestroyNotify as a GClosureNotify or GWeakNotify, a signal handler or GAsyncReadyCallback that
leaves out its last parameters). On wasm, closure notifiers, weak and toggle notifies and GTask's
callback go through ffi_wasm_call (the wpe add-on's libffi reads the function's real signature
from the program's table), every signal uses the generic (libffi) marshaller, and the closure
source's ref/unref become functions of the type they are called as.

